From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:57:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-hp-omnibook-x14: Power the DMICs from
 MIC BIAS1

The OmniBook X 14's two internal microphones are on VA DMIC0 and
DMIC1 and are powered by the WCD938x's MIC BIAS1, but the tree routes
DMIC0/1 to MIC BIAS3, as the CRD's does. DAPM then turns on the wrong
bias when the microphones are captured, so they stay unpowered and
record digital silence.

Route VA DMIC0 and DMIC1 to MIC BIAS1 and VA MIC BIAS1. With this, the
microphones record speech through the laptop's UCM profile with no
workaround, and MIC BIAS3 stays off.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi
index 73d54e6..29572c3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-hp-omnibook-x14.dtsi
@@ -173,12 +173,12 @@ sound: sound {
 				"IN1_HPHL", "HPHL_OUT",
 				"IN2_HPHR", "HPHR_OUT",
 				"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
-				"VA DMIC0", "MIC BIAS3",
-				"VA DMIC1", "MIC BIAS3",
+				"VA DMIC0", "MIC BIAS1",
+				"VA DMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
 				"VA DMIC2", "MIC BIAS1",
 				"VA DMIC3", "MIC BIAS1",
-				"VA DMIC0", "VA MIC BIAS3",
-				"VA DMIC1", "VA MIC BIAS3",
+				"VA DMIC0", "VA MIC BIAS1",
+				"VA DMIC1", "VA MIC BIAS1",
 				"VA DMIC2", "VA MIC BIAS1",
 				"VA DMIC3", "VA MIC BIAS1",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT";
-- 
